## 📘 Complete DSA Topic Roadmap (Basic to Advanced)

This roadmap outlines all essential topics you need to master for Data Structures & Algorithms, including problem-solving and interview preparation.

---

### 🟢 **Level 1: Fundamentals & Core Concepts**
  LEVEL 1 AND 2 ARE ENOUGH FOR MOST OF THE SERVICE BASED COMPANIES LIKE CAPGEMINI, INFOSYS, TCS, WIPRO, TECH MAHINDRA, ACCENTURE, COGNIZANT, HCL, IBM ETC.

1. Time & Space Complexity (Big-O Analysis)
2. Recursion   - 5 to 10 problems on basic recursion in 3 days
3. Arrays        10-15 problems on arrays in 4 days
4. Strings      - 10-15 problems on strings in 4 days
5. Mathematics & Bit Manipulation - 5 to 10 problems in 3 days
6. Sorting Algorithms (Bubble, Selection, Insertion, Merge, Quick) - 10-15 problems in 4 days
7. Searching Algorithms (Linear & Binary Search) - 5 to 10 problems in 3 days

21 days total

---

### 🔵 **Level 2: Intermediate Data Structures**

1. Hashing (HashMap, HashSet)
2. Stack
3. Queue (Linear & Circular)
4. Linked List (Singly, Doubly, Circular)
5. Sliding Window Technique
6. Two Pointers Technique
7. Prefix Sum & Difference Arrays

---

### 🟠 **Level 3: Advanced Data Structures & Algorithms**

1. Binary Trees
2. Binary Search Trees (BST)
3. Tree Traversals (Inorder, Preorder, Postorder)
4. Heap / Priority Queue
5. Tries (Prefix Trees)
6. Disjoint Set Union (Union Find)
7. Segment Tree & Binary Indexed Tree (Fenwick Tree)

---

### 🟣 **Level 4: Graphs**

1. Graph Representations (Adjacency List / Matrix)
2. DFS & BFS
3. Topological Sort
4. Shortest Path Algorithms (Dijkstra, Bellman-Ford)
5. Minimum Spanning Tree (Prim's & Kruskal's)
6. Union-Find in Graphs
7. Cycle Detection (Directed & Undirected)

---

### 🔴 **Level 5: Dynamic Programming & Advanced Algorithms**

1. 1D DP (Fibonacci, Climbing Stairs, etc.)
2. 2D DP (Knapsack, Subset Sum, etc.)
3. DP on Strings (LCS, Edit Distance)
4. DP on Trees / Graphs
5. Bitmask DP
6. Greedy Algorithms
7. Backtracking (N-Queens, Sudoku Solver)
8. Sliding Window Maximum / Monotonic Queue

---

### ⚫ **Level 6: Advanced Topics & Interview Strategies**

1. Binary Search on Answer
2. Meet in the Middle
3. Trie + Backtracking
4. Segment Tree with Lazy Propagation
5. Bit Manipulation Tricks
6. Math for CP (GCD, LCM, Sieve of Eratosthenes, Modular Arithmetic)
7. Interview Patterns & Problem Solving Techniques

---

You can build mastery by solving 20–30 quality problems per topic with increasing difficulty.

